1
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:07,575
{\an8}Controls is a special widget: one card that holds as many buttons as fit.

2
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:12,275
{\an8}Each button can do something specific, like opening another dash.

3
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:16,525
{\an8}In Widgets, open Controls to see the buttons on the card.

4
00:00:17,425 --> 00:00:23,500
{\an8}A button can open a sub dash, open an Android app on your phone, or run a MOTO-HUB action.

5
00:00:26,375 --> 00:00:29,300
{\an8}Let's open a button that links to Spotify.

6
00:00:29,775 --> 00:00:32,175
{\an8}What it does shows its current action.

7
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:38,700
{\an8}Search for another action, or pick one from the list.

8
00:00:39,525 --> 00:00:45,325
{\an8}MOTO-HUB actions include starting or stopping trip recording, and switching day and night.

9
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:49,650
{\an8}Spotify is selected because it's an app from your phone.

10
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:53,975
{\an8}All apps loads the list of apps installed on your phone.

11
00:00:54,525 --> 00:00:56,600
{\an8}Does nothing clears the button.

12
00:00:57,050 --> 00:00:59,675
{\an8}Text sets the label under the icon.

13
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,250
{\an8}Type any label you like, or leave it empty.

14
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,625
{\an8}Icon comes from the library, or you can use your own picture.

15
00:01:08,975 --> 00:01:11,050
{\an8}Background sets the fill.

16
00:01:11,275 --> 00:01:14,175
{\an8}Shape and outline adds a border, or a glow.

17
00:01:14,625 --> 00:01:19,025
{\an8}Laid out as arranges the buttons in a row, a column or a grid.

18
00:01:20,025 --> 00:01:23,400
{\an8}The difference shows when the card holds enough buttons.

19
00:01:25,275 --> 00:01:29,500
{\an8}Style sets the look of the buttons: Filled, Outline or Glass.

20
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:32,825
{\an8}Glass works well over a background photo.
